 frequent star at mega-raves in Miami and Las Vegas, appearing on immense podiums surrounded by fireworks and manic lighting shouting “I have come to party with you!” to thousands of revellers like a disco Olympian. He has been lambasted as a purveyor of trashy, vulgar songs for the masses, crude in execution and outlook. <br> <br> <br>Guetta waives dessert but I suggest I might have one. It’s actually a sign of being successful.”He began wanting to be a DJ at the age of 12. <br> <br>Blue sea and yachts are to his right, to his left is an equally blue swimming pool ringed by buff young people in afternoon repose. <br> <br>There was a moment when the music in the United States and Europe was the same. “It’s so crazy because there was no famous DJ at the time. But it was packed. “Absolutely!” he says brightly. He has two chunky rings on the fingers of one hand, rock-star jewellery. “My mum was like, ‘I’m so proud of you, you’re finally going to be an artist.’ Like, who says this?! “Of course I don’t like it, having pictures taken when I don’t look good,” he says, laughing. It will include his latest hit, “2U”, which features Justin Bieber, formerly derided as a teen-pop brat, now lauded as a credible A-lister. <br> <br>I feel like I’m the same. I was like, ‘I’m going to be rebellious, I’m going to make money.’ ” He chuckles again. It became one of the best-selling singles in chart history. Guetta was its flag-bearer. He has conquered the charts with dance-pop hits featuring some of pop’s biggest names, including Rihanna, Nicki Minaj, Usher and Sia. A chartered jet awaits him at the airport, ready to take him to club nights and summer festivals around Europe. But a final question about the troubled world beyond the Ibizan bubble — terrorism in other countries is a reason for the island’s booming tourism — elicits something of a Guetta remix of “I was never into politics but my choices when it comes to life and music were always to bring people together,” he says. At Ibiza airport, advertisements show him sporting a timepiece by the luxury watchmaker TAG Heuer. This is why I’m actually not tripping on my age. He projects the self-confidence of one who spends a good portion of his life standing above thousands of people with their hands in the air and rapture on their faces. “I’m trying to do something timeless,” he says of his music. And then when you stay, people are like — OK!” He gives a Gallic shrug and reaches for an olive from a bowl. “It’s huge. To Guetta’s detractors, the sentiment sums up his vacuity.“I never felt like I was a sellout because I have always made the music I love. And it happened, I would say, from 2009 to 2016. “I’m not especially VIP — I mean, I have money and I live this life, but I like mixing with everyone, so to me this is already the best possible answer. <br>";s:7:"keyword";s:17:"david guetta feat";s:5:"links";s:11816:"<a href='https://backyard.synpat.com/site/article.php?page=exercice-ventre-plat-femme-d%C3%A9butant-88a0eb'>Exercice Ventre Plat Femme Débutant</a>,
